indiv:Art.3 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        core:ManagementLegalRequirement ;
    ns1:SIO_000068 core:EU_AI_Act ;
    rdfs:comment "Provides core definitions (AI system, provider, deployer, high-risk AI system, general-purpose AI model) that allocate responsibilities for compliance with fairness and non-discrimination requirements. Notes: Art. 3 is definitional: notions/metrics are mapped as traceability anchors to assign fairness evidence and monitoring duties to the correct actor/artefact; mitigation techniques are mapped as control-accountability anchors (who implements and documents controls)." ;
    core:isOperationalizedBy indiv:Calibration,
        indiv:CounterfactualFairness,
        indiv:DemographicParity,
        indiv:EqualOpportunity,
        indiv:EqualizedOdds,
        indiv:StatisticalParity,
        indiv:TestFairness .

indiv:Art.4 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        core:ManagementLegalRequirement ;
    ns1:SIO_000068 core:EU_AI_Act ;
    rdfs:comment "Requires providers and deployers to take measures to ensure, to the best extent possible, a sufficient level of AI literacy for staff and other persons dealing with the operation and use of AI systems, considering their skills and the context of use. Notes: Principle/enabler: notions/metrics are mapped as training and operational interpretation anchors; the obligation is implemented via competence management (training, procedures), not via a single technical threshold." ;
    core:isOperationalizedBy indiv:Calibration,
        indiv:CounterfactualFairness,
        indiv:DemographicParity,
        indiv:EqualOpportunity,
