        indiv:RegularizationOnValueFairness,
        indiv:UserItemReRanking .

indiv:ConsistencyScore a owl:NamedIndividual,
        core:DistanceBasedFairnessMetric ;
    rdfs:comment "The aggregation potentially masks high levels of disparity for particular individuals. Very similar to Fairness through awareness, but does not require domain knowledge to define 𝑑." ;
    core:isEquivalentTo indiv:FairnessThroughAwareness ;
    core:isProposedBy papers:2013_ZEMEL ;
    core:isSuitableFor core:Prediction,
        core:Recommendation ;
    core:isUsedBy papers:2025_WALLER ;
    core:measures indiv:FairnessThroughAwareness ;
    core:refersTo core:Classification ;
    core:scientificArtifactDescription """It measures the overall level of disparity in the classification of individuals with respect to similar individuals, using the k nearest neighbours.  To do so, $yNN$ gives a value in the interval [0, 1], and the higher the value, the lower the level of disparity overall: $y_{\\mathrm{NN}} 
= 1 - \\frac{1}{N_k} \\sum_{n}
\\left| \\hat{y}_n - \\sum_{j \\in k\\text{-NN}(x_n)} \\hat{y}_j \\right| $, where $x_n$ is one of the $N$ examples in the training set.""" .

indiv:Variance a owl:NamedIndividual,
        core:AmortizedGranularityMetric,
        core:ImpactFocusedMetric,
        core:ItemFocusedMetric,
        core:SingleGranularityMetric,
        core:TreatmentFocusedMetric,
        core:UserFocusedMetric ;
    rdfs:comment "Variance is \"population size independent\" (applicable to any number of users) and satisfies \"continuity\" (any slight change in allocation shows up in the index), but affected by the unit of measure. Example: if an algorithm gives 1,3,5 dollars respectively to three users, variance is 4. If it gives 100,300,500 pennies each, variance is 40,000 (10000 worse than before) [1984_JAIN]. Coefficent of variation (i.e., variance/mean) would not be affected by the change of unit of measure. Furthermore, variance (and Coefficent of variation) does not satisfy boundedness (the index should be bounded between 0 and 1 for comparrison and interpretability)" ;
    core:isProposedBy papers:2017_LIN ;
    core:isSuitableFor core:Recommendation ;
    core:isUsedBy papers:2018_KAMISHIMA,
        papers:2019_RASTEGARPANAH,
        papers:2021_WU ;
    core:measures indiv:FairRecommendationForCustomer,
        indiv:QualityWeightedFairness,
        indiv:UniformFairness ;
    core:refersTo core:ScoringRegression .

