indiv:ControlOffensiveTokens a owl:NamedIndividual,
        core:DecisionTimeConstrainedDecisioning ;
    core:scientificArtifactDescription "use word- or ngram-blocking during decoding, prohibiting the use of tokens from an offensive word list. The authors identify control tokens using a classifier that measures offensiveness, bias, and other potential harms in text. The control tokens can be appended to the input during inference to control model generation." .

indiv:REALTOXICITYPROMPTS a owl:NamedIndividual,
        core:OutputRewriting ;
    core:scientificArtifactDescription "adaptive pretraining on non-toxic data: increase the likelihood of non-toxic tokens, adding a (non-)toxicity score to the logits over the vocabulary before normalization, ans use word- or ngram-blocking during decoding, prohibiting the use of tokens from an offensive word list" .

indiv:AddNonToxicExamples a owl:NamedIndividual,
        core:SyntheticData ;
    core:scientificArtifactDescription "Add non-toxic examples for groups disproportionately represented with toxicity, until the distribution between toxic and non-toxic examples is balanced across groups." .

indiv:BlocklistDocumentRemoval a owl:NamedIndividual,
        core:Cleaning ;
    core:scientificArtifactDescription "Removal of biased instances, such as derogatory language: coarse word-level technique, removing all documents containing any words on a blocklist." .

indiv:LogLikeDocumentRemoval a owl:NamedIndividual,
        core:Cleaning ;
    core:scientificArtifactDescription "Append to each document a phrase representative of an undesirable harm, such as racism or hate speech, and then use a pre-trained model to compute the conditional log-likelihood of the modified documents. Documents with high loglikelihoods are removed from the training set." .

indiv:PredictiveEquality a owl:NamedIndividual,
        core:ObservationalFairnessNotion,
        core:SeparationFairnessNotion ;
    rdfs:comment "a predictor that satisfy both predictive equality and equal opportunity, also satisfy equalized odds." ;
    core:isEquivalentTo indiv:FalsePositiveErrorRateBalance ;
    core:isProposedBy papers:2016_HARDT ;
    core:isSuitableFor core:Conversation,
        core:Prediction ;
    core:refersTo core:Classification,
        core:TextGeneration .

indiv:AdversarialFDP a owl:NamedIndividual,
        core:AdversarialLearning ;
    core:scientificArtifactDescription "The adversary seeks to determine whether the training process is fair, and when not, feedback from the adversary is used to improve the model. Uses FDR as a fariness metric within the adversary to apply feedback for model tuning as a form of in-processing: the adversary penalizes the model if a sensitive variable is predictable from the dependent variable." .

indiv:PerceptronForUnawareness a owl:NamedIndividual,
        core:Adapters ;
    core:scientificArtifactDescription "creates an adapter network by training a single-layer multilayer perceptron with the objective of removing protected attributes, with an additional fusion module to combine the original pretrained model with the adapter." .

indiv:ConditionalStatisticalParity a owl:NamedIndividual,
        core:IndependenceFairnessNotion,
        core:ObservationalFairnessNotion ;
    rdfs:comment "Conditional statistical parity is closely related to the idea of fairness through blindness (i.e., unawareness[Ndr]), in which one attempts to create fair algorithms by prohibiting use of protected attributes, such as race. However, as frequently noted, it is difficult to restrict to “legitimate” features that do not at least partially correlate with race and other protected attributes, and so one cannot be completely “blind” to the sensitive information. Moreover, unlike the other definitions of fairness, this one does not necessarily re- duce racial disparities. Conditional statistical parity mitigates these limitations of the blindness approach while preserving its intuitive appeal. [2017_CORBETT_DAVIES]" ;
    core:extends indiv:FairnessThroughUnawareness,
        indiv:StatisticalParity ;
    core:isProposedBy papers:2017_CORBETT_DAVIES ;
    core:isSuitableFor core:Conversation,
        core:Prediction,
        core:Recommendation ;
    core:refersTo core:Classification,
        core:TextGeneration .

indiv:CalibratedReRanking a owl:NamedIndividual,
        core:CalibrationBasedMitigation ;
    core:scientificArtifactDescription "Calibrated recommendation through maximal marginal relevance" .

indiv:ListReAdjustment a owl:NamedIndividual,
        core:Reranking ;
    core:scientificArtifactDescription "Re-ranking method based on maximum flow: iteratively adds high-quality items that have low visibility or items from suppliers with low exposure to the users’ final recommendation lists." .

indiv:RegularizationOnANOVA a owl:NamedIndividual,
        core:FairnessRegularization ;
    core:scientificArtifactDescription "Use F-statistic of ANOVA in the the loss function as regularization term to calibrate the parity of prediction errors across different market segments." .

indiv:RegularizationOnValueFairness a owl:NamedIndividual,
        core:FairnessRegularization ;
    core:scientificArtifactDescription "Use fairness metrics (e.g., value fairness) as fair regularization" .

indiv:UserItemReRanking a owl:NamedIndividual,
        core:Reranking ;
    core:scientificArtifactDescription "Re-ranking  for both user fairness and item fairness" .

indiv:IndividualFairness a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    owl:sameAs indiv:FairnessThroughAwareness .

indiv:AugmentedAntidoteData a owl:NamedIndividual,
        core:CounterfactualAugmentation ;
    core:scientificArtifactDescription "Add antidote data to the training data" .

indiv:CDA a owl:NamedIndividual,
        core:CounterfactualAugmentation ;
    core:scientificArtifactDescription "Use CDA to mitigate occupation-gender bias, creating matched pairs by flipping gendered (e.g., “he” and “she”) or definitionally gendered (e.g., “king” and “queen”) words, while preserving grammatical and semantic correctness, under the definition that an unbiased model should consider each sentence in a pair equally." .

indiv:ReSamplingProtectedGroup a owl:NamedIndividual,
        core:StratifiedSampling ;
    core:scientificArtifactDescription "Adjust the proportion of the protected group by resampling" .

indiv:FairnessThroughAwareness a owl:NamedIndividual,
        core:IndividualFairnessNotion,
        core:ObservationalFairnessNotion ;
    owl:sameAs indiv:IndividualFairness ;
    core:isEquivalentTo indiv:IndividualFairness ;
    core:isMeasuredBy indiv:ConsistencyScore,
        indiv:IndividualConsistencyScore,
        indiv:LowIndividualConsistencyCount,
        indiv:ProportionalConsistencyScore,
        indiv:RelativeLInfiniteMetric,
        indiv:SimilarityRobustnessOfIndividualConsistency,
        indiv:TotalVariationNorm ;
    core:isProposedBy papers:2012_DWORK ;
    core:isSuitableFor core:Prediction,
        core:Recommendation ;
    core:isUsedBy papers:2018_YONA,
        papers:2019_LAHOTI,
        papers:2020_YUROCHKIN,
        papers:2025_GAO ;
    core:refersTo core:Classification ;
    core:scientificArtifactDescription """An algorithm is fair if it gives similar predictions to similar individuals
Awareness is based on the Lipschitz condition, which requires that any two individuals 
$x$ and $y$ at distance $d(x,y) \\in [0,1]$ map to distributions $M(x)$ and $M(y)$, respectively, such that the statistical distance between them is at most $d(x,y)$:
\\[
D(M(x_1), M(x_2)) \\le d(x_1, x_2), 
\\quad \\forall x_1, x_2 \\in E .
\\]

Here, $M(x)$ denotes the probability distribution of the output for individual $x$, 
$E$ is a dataset, $D(\\cdot,\\cdot)$ returns the statistical distance between 
$M(x_1)$ and $M(x_2)$, and $d(\\cdot,\\cdot)$ denotes a distance between individuals 
$x_1$ and $x_2$, defined using a pre-specified, domain-dependent notion of similarity.
\\cite{2025_WALLER}""" .

indiv:DemographicParity a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    owl:sameAs indiv:StatisticalParity .

indiv:EqualizedOdds a owl:NamedIndividual,
        core:ObservationalFairnessNotion,
        core:SeparationFairnessNotion ;
    rdfs:comment "for NLP classification tasks, or tasks with a superimposed classifier, traditional fairness definitions like equalized odds or statistical parity MAY be used without modification[2024_Gallegos]. Extends Equal opportunity  and Predictive equality  i.e., if you satisfy Equalized odds, than you also satisfy Equal opportunity. It also extends Overall accuracy equality because if you achieve equalized odds, then you have equal accuracy." ;
    core:extends indiv:EqualOpportunity,
        indiv:OverallAccuracyEquality,
        indiv:PredictiveEquality ;
    core:isEquivalentTo indiv:ConditionalProcedureAccuracyEquality ;
    core:isMeasuredBy indiv:OutcomeUnfairness ;
    core:isProposedBy papers:2021_BERK ;
    core:isSuitableFor core:Conversation,
        core:Prediction ;
    core:refersTo core:Classification,
        core:TextGeneration .

